    <article class="docs-prose">
      <h1 id="cnf-image-based-upgrade" class="group scroll-mt-20">Performing an image-based upgrade for single-node OpenShift clusters with the Lifecycle Agent<a href="#cnf-image-based-upgrade" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p>You can use the Lifecycle Agent to do a manual image-based upgrade of a single-node OpenShift cluster.</p>
      <p>When you deploy the Lifecycle Agent on a cluster, an <code>ImageBasedUpgrade</code> CR is automatically created. You update this CR to specify the image repository of the seed image and to move through the different stages.</p>
      <h2 id="ztp-image-based-upgrade-prep_cnf-non-gitops" class="group scroll-mt-20">Moving to the Prep stage of the image-based upgrade with Lifecycle Agent<a href="#ztp-image-based-upgrade-prep_cnf-non-gitops" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">When you deploy the Lifecycle Agent on a cluster, the Lifecycle Agent automatically creates an <code>ImageBasedUpgrade</code> custom resource (CR).</p>
      <p>After you create all the resources that you need during the upgrade, you can move on to the <code>Prep</code> stage. For more information, see the "Creating ConfigMap objects for the image-based upgrade with Lifecycle Agent" section.</p>
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>In a disconnected environment, if the seed cluster’s release image registry is different from the target cluster’s release image registry, you must create an <code>ImageDigestMirrorSet</code> (IDMS) resource to configure alternative mirrored repository locations. For more information, see "Configuring image registry repository mirroring".</p>
          <p>You can retrieve the release registry used in the seed image by running the following command:</p>
          <CodeBlock code={"$ skopeo inspect docker://<imagename> | jq -r '.Labels.\"com.openshift.lifecycle-agent.seed_cluster_info\" | fromjson | .release_registry'"} lang="terminal" />
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul><li>You have created resources to back up and restore your clusters.</li></ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Check that you have patched your <code>ImageBasedUpgrade</code> CR:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: lca.openshift.io/v1\nkind: ImageBasedUpgrade\nmetadata:\n  name: upgrade\nspec:\n  stage: Idle\n  seedImageRef:\n    version: <target_version>\n    image: <seed_container_image>\n    pullSecretRef: <seed_pull_secret>\n  autoRollbackOnFailure: {}\n    initMonitorTimeoutSeconds: <initMonitorTimeoutSeconds>\n  extraManifests:\n  - name: example-extra-manifests-cm\n    namespace: openshift-lifecycle-agent\n  - name: example-catalogsources-cm\n    namespace: openshift-lifecycle-agent\n  oadpContent:\n  - name: oadp-cm-example\n    namespace: openshift-adp"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;target_version&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Target platform version. The value must match the version of the seed image.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;seed_container_image&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Repository where the target cluster can pull the seed image from.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;seed_pull_secret&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Reference to a secret with credentials to pull container images if the images are in a private registry.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;initMonitorTimeoutSeconds&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Optional: Time frame in seconds to roll back if the upgrade does not complete within that time frame after the first reboot. If not defined or set to <code>0</code>, the Lifecycle Agent uses the default value of <code>1800</code> seconds (30 minutes).</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>extraManifests</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Optional: List of <code>ConfigMap</code> resources. These resources contain your custom catalog sources to retain after the upgrade and any extra manifests that the seed image does not include.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>oadpContent</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>List of <code>ConfigMap</code> resources that contain the OADP <code>Backup</code> and <code>Restore</code> CRs.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      </li>
      <li>
      To start the <code>Prep</code> stage, change the value of the <code>stage</code> field to <code>Prep</code> in the <code>ImageBasedUpgrade</code> CR by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc patch imagebasedupgrades.lca.openshift.io upgrade -p='{\"spec\": {\"stage\": \"Prep\"}}' --type=merge -n openshift-lifecycle-agent"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>If you include <code>ConfigMap</code> objects for OADP resources and extra manifests, Lifecycle Agent validates the specified <code>ConfigMap</code> objects during the <code>Prep</code> stage.</p>
      <p>The following issues might occur:</p>
      <ul>
      <li>Validation warnings or errors if the Lifecycle Agent detects any issues with the <code>extraManifests</code> parameters.</li>
      <li>Validation errors if the Lifecycle Agent detects any issues with the <code>oadpContent</code> parameters.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Validation warnings do not block the <code>Upgrade</code> stage but you must decide if it is safe to proceed with the upgrade. These warnings, for example missing custom resource definitions (CRDs), namespaces, or dry run failures, update the <code>status.conditions</code> for the <code>Prep</code> stage and <code>annotation</code> fields in the <code>ImageBasedUpgrade</code> CR with details about the warning. The following example shows these details:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"# ...\nmetadata:\nannotations:\n  extra-manifest.lca.openshift.io/validation-warning: '...'\n# ..."} lang="yaml" />
      <p>However, validation errors, such as adding <code>MachineConfig</code> or Operator manifests to extra manifests, cause the <code>Prep</code> stage to fail and block the <code>Upgrade</code> stage.</p>
      <p>When the validations pass, the cluster creates a new <code>ostree</code> stateroot, which involves pulling and unpacking the seed image, and running host-level commands. Finally, the Lifecycle Agent precaches all the required images on the target cluster.</p>
      </li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Verification</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      Check the status of the <code>ImageBasedUpgrade</code> CR by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get ibu -o yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>The following example shows a successful <code>Prep</code> stage:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"  conditions:\n  - lastTransitionTime: \"2024-01-01T09:00:00Z\"\n    message: In progress\n    observedGeneration: 13\n    reason: InProgress\n    status: \"False\"\n    type: Idle\n  - lastTransitionTime: \"2024-01-01T09:00:00Z\"\n    message: Prep completed\n    observedGeneration: 13\n    reason: Completed\n    status: \"False\"\n    type: PrepInProgress\n  - lastTransitionTime: \"2024-01-01T09:00:00Z\"\n    message: Prep stage completed successfully\n    observedGeneration: 13\n    reason: Completed\n    status: \"True\"\n    type: PrepCompleted\n  observedGeneration: 13\n  validNextStages:\n  - Idle\n  - Upgrade"} lang="yaml" />
      </li>
      </ul>
      <section class="related-resources _additional-resources">
      <p class="related-resources-title">Additional resources</p>
      <ul>
      <li><a href="/openshift-docs-markdown/edge_computing/image_based_upgrade/preparing_for_image_based_upgrade/cnf-image-based-upgrade-prep-resources#cnf-image-based-upgrade-prep-resources">Creating ConfigMap objects for the image-based upgrade with Lifecycle Agent</a></li>
      <li><a href="/openshift-docs-markdown/openshift_images/image-configuration#images-configuration-registry-mirror-configuring_image-configuration">Configuring image registry repository mirroring</a></li>
      </ul>
      </section>
      <h2 id="cnf-image-based-upgrade-with-backup_cnf-non-gitops" class="group scroll-mt-20">Moving to the Upgrade stage of the image-based upgrade with Lifecycle Agent<a href="#cnf-image-based-upgrade-with-backup_cnf-non-gitops" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">After you generate the seed image and complete the <code>Prep</code> stage, you can upgrade the target cluster. During the upgrade process, the OADP Operator creates a backup of the artifacts specified in the OADP custom resources (CRs), then the Lifecycle Agent upgrades the cluster.</p>
      <p>If the upgrade fails or stops, the Lifecycle Agent initiates an automatic rollback. If you have an issue after the upgrade, you can perform a manual rollback. For more information about manual rollback, see "Moving to the Rollback stage of the image-based upgrade with Lifecycle Agent".</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul><li>You have completed the <code>Prep</code> stage.</li></ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      To move to the <code>Upgrade</code> stage, change the value of the <code>stage</code> field to <code>Upgrade</code> in the <code>ImageBasedUpgrade</code> CR by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc patch imagebasedupgrades.lca.openshift.io upgrade -p='{\"spec\": {\"stage\": \"Upgrade\"}}' --type=merge"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Check the status of the <code>ImageBasedUpgrade</code> CR by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get ibu -o yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>The following example shows an upgrade in progress:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"status:\n  conditions:\n  - lastTransitionTime: \"2024-01-01T09:00:00Z\"\n    message: In progress\n    observedGeneration: 5\n    reason: InProgress\n    status: \"False\"\n    type: Idle\n  - lastTransitionTime: \"2024-01-01T09:00:00Z\"\n    message: Prep completed\n    observedGeneration: 5\n    reason: Completed\n    status: \"False\"\n    type: PrepInProgress\n  - lastTransitionTime: \"2024-01-01T09:00:00Z\"\n    message: Prep completed successfully\n    observedGeneration: 5\n    reason: Completed\n    status: \"True\"\n    type: PrepCompleted\n  - lastTransitionTime: \"2024-01-01T09:00:00Z\"\n    message: |-\n      Waiting for system to stabilize: one or more health checks failed\n        - one or more ClusterOperators not yet ready: authentication\n        - one or more MachineConfigPools not yet ready: master\n        - one or more ClusterServiceVersions not yet ready: sriov-fec.v2.8.0\n    observedGeneration: 1\n    reason: InProgress\n    status: \"True\"\n    type: UpgradeInProgress\n  observedGeneration: 1\n  rollbackAvailabilityExpiration: \"2024-05-19T14:01:52Z\"\n  validNextStages:\n  - Rollback"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>The OADP Operator creates a backup of the data specified in the OADP <code>Backup</code> and <code>Restore</code> CRs and the target cluster reboots.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
      Monitor the status of the CR by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get ibu -o yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      After the upgrade, complete the changes by patching the value of the <code>stage</code> field to <code>Idle</code> in the <code>ImageBasedUpgrade</code> CR by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc patch imagebasedupgrades.lca.openshift.io upgrade -p='{\"spec\": {\"stage\": \"Idle\"}}' --type=merge"} lang="terminal" />
      <Alert variant="info" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Important</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>You cannot roll back the changes once you move to the <code>Idle</code> stage after an upgrade.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      <p>The Lifecycle Agent deletes all resources created during the upgrade process.</p>
      </li>
      <li>You can remove the OADP Operator and its configuration files after a successful upgrade. For more information, see "Deleting Operators from a cluster".</li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Verification</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Check the status of the <code>ImageBasedUpgrade</code> CR by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get ibu -o yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>The following example shows a completed upgrade:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"status:\n  conditions:\n  - lastTransitionTime: \"2024-01-01T09:00:00Z\"\n    message: In progress\n    observedGeneration: 5\n    reason: InProgress\n    status: \"False\"\n    type: Idle\n  - lastTransitionTime: \"2024-01-01T09:00:00Z\"\n    message: Prep completed\n    observedGeneration: 5\n    reason: Completed\n    status: \"False\"\n    type: PrepInProgress\n  - lastTransitionTime: \"2024-01-01T09:00:00Z\"\n    message: Prep completed successfully\n    observedGeneration: 5\n    reason: Completed\n    status: \"True\"\n    type: PrepCompleted\n  - lastTransitionTime: \"2024-01-01T09:00:00Z\"\n    message: Upgrade completed\n    observedGeneration: 1\n    reason: Completed\n    status: \"False\"\n    type: UpgradeInProgress\n  - lastTransitionTime: \"2024-01-01T09:00:00Z\"\n    message: Upgrade completed\n    observedGeneration: 1\n    reason: Completed\n    status: \"True\"\n    type: UpgradeCompleted\n  observedGeneration: 1\n  rollbackAvailabilityExpiration: \"2024-01-01T09:00:00Z\"\n  validNextStages:\n  - Idle\n  - Rollback"} lang="yaml" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Check the status of the cluster restoration by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get restores -n openshift-adp -o custom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name,Status:.status.phase,Reason:.status.failureReason"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>The following example shows completed restores:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"NAME             Status      Reason\nacm-klusterlet   Completed   <none>\napache-app       Completed   <none>\nlocalvolume      Completed   <none>"} lang="terminal" />
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>The <code>acm-klusterlet</code> is specific to RHACM environments only.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      </li>
      </ol>
      <section class="related-resources _additional-resources">
      <p class="related-resources-title">Additional resources</p>
      <ul>
      <li><a href="/openshift-docs-markdown/edge_computing/image_based_upgrade/cnf-image-based-upgrade-base#cnf-image-based-upgrade-rollback_cnf-non-gitops">Moving to the Rollback stage of the image-based upgrade with Lifecycle Agent</a></li>
      <li><a href="/openshift-docs-markdown/operators/admin/olm-deleting-operators-from-cluster#olm-deleting-operators-from-cluster">Deleting Operators from a cluster</a></li>
      </ul>
      </section>
      <h2 id="cnf-image-based-upgrade-rollback_cnf-non-gitops" class="group scroll-mt-20">Moving to the Rollback stage of the image-based upgrade with Lifecycle Agent<a href="#cnf-image-based-upgrade-rollback_cnf-non-gitops" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">The Lifecycle Agent initiates an automatic rollback if the upgrade does not complete within the time frame specified in the <code>initMonitorTimeoutSeconds</code> field after rebooting, as shown in the following example:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: lca.openshift.io/v1\nkind: ImageBasedUpgrade\nmetadata:\n  name: upgrade\nspec:\n  stage: Idle\n  seedImageRef:\n    version: 4.15.2\n    image: <seed_container_image>\n  autoRollbackOnFailure: {}\n#    initMonitorTimeoutSeconds: <initMonitorTimeoutSeconds>\n# ..."} lang="yaml" />
      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;initMonitorTimeoutSeconds&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Optional: The time frame in seconds to roll back if the upgrade does not complete within that time frame after the first reboot. If not defined or set to <code>0</code>, the Lifecycle Agent uses the default value of <code>1800</code> seconds (30 minutes).</p></dd>
      </dl>
      <p>You can manually roll back the changes if you see unresolvable issues after an upgrade.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>You have logged into the hub cluster as a user with <code>cluster-admin</code> privileges.</li>
      <li>You ensured that the control plane certificates on the original stateroot are valid. If the certificates expired, see "Recovering from expired control plane certificates".</li>
      </ul>
      <Alert variant="warning" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Warning</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>If you choose to upgrade a recently installed single-node OpenShift cluster for example, for testing purposes, you have a limited rollback time frame of 24 hours or less. You can verify the rollback time by checking the <code>rollbackAvailabilityExpiration</code> field of the <code>ImageBasedUpgrade</code> custom resource.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      To move to the rollback stage, patch the value of the <code>stage</code> field to <code>Rollback</code> in the <code>ImageBasedUpgrade</code> CR by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc patch imagebasedupgrades.lca.openshift.io upgrade -p='{\"spec\": {\"stage\": \"Rollback\"}}' --type=merge"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>The Lifecycle Agent reboots the cluster with the previously installed version of OpenShift Container Platform and restores the applications.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
      After reviewing the changes, complete the rollback by patching the value of the <code>stage</code> field to <code>Idle</code> in the <code>ImageBasedUpgrade</code> CR by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc patch imagebasedupgrades.lca.openshift.io upgrade -p='{\"spec\": {\"stage\": \"Idle\"}}' --type=merge -n openshift-lifecycle-agent"} lang="terminal" />
      <Alert variant="warning" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Warning</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>If you move to the <code>Idle</code> stage after a rollback, the Lifecycle Agent cleans up resources that you can use to troubleshoot a failed upgrade.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      </li>
      </ol>
      <section class="related-resources _additional-resources">
      <p class="related-resources-title">Additional resources</p>
      <ul><li><a href="/openshift-docs-markdown/backup_and_restore/control_plane_backup_and_restore/disaster_recovery/scenario-3-expired-certs#dr-scenario-3-recovering-expired-certs_dr-recovering-expired-certs">Recovering from expired control plane certificates</a></li></ul>
      </section>
      <h2 id="cnf-image-based-upgrade-troubleshooting_cnf-non-gitops" class="group scroll-mt-20">Troubleshooting image-based upgrades with Lifecycle Agent<a href="#cnf-image-based-upgrade-troubleshooting_cnf-non-gitops" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">Perform troubleshooting steps on the managed clusters to resolve any issues.</p>
      <Alert variant="info" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Important</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>If you are using the <code>ImageBasedGroupUpgrade</code> CR to upgrade your clusters, ensure that you update the <code>lcm.openshift.io/ibgu-&lt;stage&gt;-completed</code> or <code>lcm.openshift.io/ibgu-&lt;stage&gt;-failed</code> cluster labels properly after performing troubleshooting or recovery steps on the managed clusters. This ensures that the TALM continues to manage the image-based upgrade for the cluster.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      <h3 id="cnf-image-based-upgrade-troubleshooting-must-gather_cnf-non-gitops" class="group scroll-mt-20">Collecting logs<a href="#cnf-image-based-upgrade-troubleshooting-must-gather_cnf-non-gitops" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
      <p>You can use the <code>oc adm must-gather</code> CLI to collect information for debugging and troubleshooting.</p>
      <p>To collect data about the Operators, run the following command:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"$  oc adm must-gather \\\n  --dest-dir=must-gather/tmp \\\n  --image=$(oc -n openshift-lifecycle-agent get deployment.apps/lifecycle-agent-controller-manager -o jsonpath='{.spec.template.spec.containers[?(@.name == \"manager\")].image}') \\\n  --image=quay.io/konveyor/oadp-must-gather:latest \\//\n  --image=quay.io/openshift/origin-must-gather:latest"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>Where:</p>
      <ul>
      <li><code>--image=quay.io/konveyor/oadp-must-gather:latest</code>: Optional: Add this option if you need to gather more information from the OADP Operator.</li>
      <li><code>--image=quay.io/openshift/origin-must-gather:latest</code>: Optional: Add this option if you need to gather more information from the SR-IOV Operator.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3 id="cnf-image-based-upgrade-troubleshooting-manual-cleanup_cnf-non-gitops" class="group scroll-mt-20"><code>AbortFailed</code> or <code>FinalizeFailed</code> error<a href="#cnf-image-based-upgrade-troubleshooting-manual-cleanup_cnf-non-gitops" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold">Issue</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground">
      <p>During the finalization stage or when you stop the process at the <code>Prep</code> stage, Lifecycle Agent cleans up the following resources:</p>
      <ul>
      <li>Stateroot that is no longer required</li>
      <li>Precaching resources</li>
      <li>OADP CRs</li>
      <li><code>ImageBasedUpgrade</code> CR</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If the Lifecycle Agent fails to clean up these resources, it transitions to the <code>AbortFailed</code> or <code>FinalizeFailed</code> states. The condition message and log show the steps that failed, as shown in the following example:</p>
      <p>Example error message:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"message: failed to delete all the backup CRs. Perform cleanup manually then add 'lca.openshift.io/manual-cleanup-done' annotation to ibu CR to transition back to Idle\n      observedGeneration: 5\n      reason: AbortFailed\n      status: \"False\"\n      type: Idle"} lang="yaml" />
      </dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold">Resolution</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground">
      <ol>
      <li>Inspect the logs to find the reason for failure.</li>
      <li>To prompt Lifecycle Agent to retry the cleanup, add the <code>lca.openshift.io/manual-cleanup-done</code> annotation to the <code>ImageBasedUpgrade</code> CR.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>After observing this annotation, Lifecycle Agent retries the cleanup and, if it is successful, the <code>ImageBasedUpgrade</code> stage transitions to <code>Idle</code>.</p>
      <p>If the cleanup fails again, you can manually clean up the resources.</p>
      </dd>
      </dl>
      <h3 id="cnf-image-based-upgrade-troubleshooting-stateroot_cnf-non-gitops" class="group scroll-mt-20">Cleaning up stateroot manually<a href="#cnf-image-based-upgrade-troubleshooting-stateroot_cnf-non-gitops" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold">Issue</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Stopping at the <code>Prep</code> stage, Lifecycle Agent cleans up the new stateroot. When finalizing after a successful upgrade or a rollback, Lifecycle Agent cleans up the old stateroot. If this step fails, you must inspect the logs to decide why the failure occurred.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold">Resolution</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground">
      <ol><li>Check if there are any existing deployments in the stateroot by running the following command:</li></ol>
      <CodeBlock code={"$ ostree admin status"} lang="terminal" />
      <ol><li>If there are any, clean up the existing deployment by running the following command:</li></ol>
      <CodeBlock code={"$ ostree admin undeploy <index_of_deployment>"} lang="terminal" />
      <ol><li>After cleaning up all the deployments of the stateroot, wipe the stateroot directory by running the following commands:</li></ol>
      <Alert variant="warning" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Warning</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>Ensure that the booted deployment is not in this stateroot.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      <CodeBlock code={"$ stateroot=\"<stateroot_to_delete>\""} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"$ unshare -m /bin/sh -c \"mount -o remount,rw /sysroot && rm -rf /sysroot/ostree/deploy/${stateroot}\""} lang="terminal" />
      </dd>
      </dl>
      <h3 id="cnf-image-based-upgrade-troubleshooting-oadp-resources_cnf-non-gitops" class="group scroll-mt-20">Cleaning up OADP resources manually<a href="#cnf-image-based-upgrade-troubleshooting-oadp-resources_cnf-non-gitops" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold">Issue</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Automatic cleanup of OADP resources can fail due to connection issues between Lifecycle Agent and the S3 backend. By restoring the connection and adding the <code>lca.openshift.io/manual-cleanup-done</code> annotation, the Lifecycle Agent can successfully cleanup backup resources.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold">Resolution</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground">
      <ol><li>Check the backend connectivity by running the following command:</li></ol>
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get backupstoragelocations.velero.io -n openshift-adp"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>The following example shows successful backend connectivity:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"NAME                          PHASE       LAST VALIDATED   AGE   DEFAULT\ndataprotectionapplication-1   Available   33s              8d    true"} lang="terminal" />
      <ol><li>Remove all backup resources and then add the <code>lca.openshift.io/manual-cleanup-done</code> annotation to the <code>ImageBasedUpgrade</code> CR.</li></ol>
      </dd>
      </dl>
      <h3 id="cnf-image-based-upgrade-troubleshooting-lvms_cnf-non-gitops" class="group scroll-mt-20">LVM Storage volume contents not restored<a href="#cnf-image-based-upgrade-troubleshooting-lvms_cnf-non-gitops" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
      <p>When you use LVM Storage to configure dynamic persistent volume storage, LVM Storage might not restore the persistent volume contents if you have configured it incorrectly.</p>
      <h3 id="cnf-image-based-upgrade-troubleshooting-lvms-backup_cnf-non-gitops" class="group scroll-mt-20">Missing LVM Storage-related fields in Backup CR<a href="#cnf-image-based-upgrade-troubleshooting-lvms-backup_cnf-non-gitops" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold">Issue</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground">
      <p>Your <code>Backup</code> CRs might be missing fields that you need to restore your persistent volumes. You can check for events in your application pod to decide if you have this issue by running the following:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc describe pod <your_app_name>"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>The following example output shows a pod failing due to missing LVM Storage-related fields in the <code>Backup</code> CR:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"Events:\n  Type     Reason            Age                From               Message\n  ----     ------            ----               ----               -------\n  Warning  FailedScheduling  58s (x2 over 66s)  default-scheduler  0/1 nodes are available: pod has unbound immediate PersistentVolumeClaims. preemption: 0/1 nodes are available: 1 Preemption is not helpful for scheduling..\n  Normal   Scheduled         56s                default-scheduler  Successfully assigned default/db-1234 to sno1.example.lab\n  Warning  FailedMount       24s (x7 over 55s)  kubelet            MountVolume.SetUp failed for volume \"pvc-1234\" : rpc error: code = Unknown desc = VolumeID is not found"} lang="terminal" />
      </dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold">Resolution</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground">
      <p>You must include <code>logicalvolumes.topolvm.io</code> in the application <code>Backup</code> CR. Without this resource, the application restores its persistent volume claims and persistent volume manifests correctly, however, the <code>logicalvolume</code> associated with this persistent volume is not restored properly after pivot. The following example shows a correctly configured <code>Backup</code> CR:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: velero.io/v1\nkind: Backup\nmetadata:\n  labels:\n    velero.io/storage-location: default\n  name: small-app\n  namespace: openshift-adp\nspec:\n  includedNamespaces:\n  - test\n  includedNamespaceScopedResources:\n  - secrets\n  - persistentvolumeclaims\n  - deployments\n  - statefulsets\n  includedClusterScopedResources:\n  - persistentVolumes\n  - volumesnapshotcontents\n  - logicalvolumes.topolvm.io"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>To restore the persistent volumes for your application, you must configure the <code>includedClusterScopedResources</code> section as shown.</p>
      </dd>
      </dl>
      <h3 id="cnf-image-based-upgrade-troubleshooting-lvms-restore_cnf-non-gitops" class="group scroll-mt-20">Missing LVM Storage-related fields in Restore CR<a href="#cnf-image-based-upgrade-troubleshooting-lvms-restore_cnf-non-gitops" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold">Issue</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>LVM Storage restores the expected resources for the applications but it does not preserve the persistent volume contents after upgrading.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      <ol>
      <li>
      List the persistent volumes for you applications by running the following command before pivot:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get pv,pvc,logicalvolumes.topolvm.io -A"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>The following shows the output before pivot:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"NAME                        CAPACITY   ACCESS MODES   RECLAIM POLICY   STATUS   CLAIM            STORAGECLASS   REASON   AGE\npersistentvolume/pvc-1234   1Gi        RWO            Retain           Bound    default/pvc-db   lvms-vg1                4h45m\n\nNAMESPACE   NAME                           STATUS   VOLUME     CAPACITY   ACCESS MODES   STORAGECLASS   AGE\ndefault     persistentvolumeclaim/pvc-db   Bound    pvc-1234   1Gi        RWO            lvms-vg1       4h45m\n\nNAMESPACE   NAME                                AGE\n            logicalvolume.topolvm.io/pvc-1234   4h45m"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      List the persistent volumes for you applications by running the following command after pivot:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get pv,pvc,logicalvolumes.topolvm.io -A"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>The following shows the output after pivot:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"NAME                        CAPACITY   ACCESS MODES   RECLAIM POLICY   STATUS   CLAIM            STORAGECLASS   REASON   AGE\npersistentvolume/pvc-1234   1Gi        RWO            Delete           Bound    default/pvc-db   lvms-vg1                19s\n\nNAMESPACE   NAME                           STATUS   VOLUME     CAPACITY   ACCESS MODES   STORAGECLASS   AGE\ndefault     persistentvolumeclaim/pvc-db   Bound    pvc-1234   1Gi        RWO            lvms-vg1       19s\n\nNAMESPACE   NAME                                AGE\n            logicalvolume.topolvm.io/pvc-1234   18s"} lang="terminal" />
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold">Resolution</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>The reason for this issue is that the <code>logicalvolume</code> status is not preserved in the <code>Restore</code> CR. This status is important because Velero requires this status to reference the volumes that you must preserve after pivoting. You must include the following fields in the application <code>Restore</code> CR, as shown in the following example:</p></dd>
      </dl>
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: velero.io/v1\nkind: Restore\nmetadata:\n  name: sample-vote-app\n  namespace: openshift-adp\n  labels:\n    velero.io/storage-location: default\n  annotations:\n    lca.openshift.io/apply-wave: \"3\"\nspec:\n  backupName:\n    sample-vote-app\n  restorePVs: <restore_pvs>\n  restoreStatus:\n    includedResources:\n      - logicalvolumes"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>where: <code>&lt;restore_pvs&gt;</code>:: To preserve the persistent volumes for your application, you must set <code>restorePVs</code> to <code>true</code>. <code>restoreStatus</code>:: To preserve the persistent volumes for your application, you must configure this field as shown.</p>
      </li>
      </ol>
      <h3 id="cnf-image-based-upgrade-troubleshooting-debugging-oadp-crs_cnf-non-gitops" class="group scroll-mt-20">Debugging failed Backup and Restore CRs<a href="#cnf-image-based-upgrade-troubleshooting-debugging-oadp-crs_cnf-non-gitops" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold">Issue</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>The backup or restoration of artifacts failed.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold">Resolution</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>You can debug <code>Backup</code> and <code>Restore</code> CRs and retrieve logs with the OADP CLI. The OADP CLI offers more detailed information than the OpenShift CLI tool.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Describe the <code>Backup</code> CR that has errors by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc oadp backup describe backup-acm-klusterlet -n openshift-adp --details"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Describe the <code>Restore</code> CR that has errors by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc oadp restore describe restore-acm-klusterlet -n openshift-adp --details"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Download the backed up resources to a local directory by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc oadp backup download backup-acm-klusterlet -n openshift-adp -o ~/backup-acm-klusterlet.tar.gz"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
    </article>
